    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0711" n="693" xml:id="pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.00/3–647</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Deputy Director of the Office
                        of European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hickerson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-06">March 6, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Jack</hi>: Prior to the Secretary’s arrival in
                    Paris this morning I prepared a brief and rather general memorandum on the
                    present French picture as we see it at this juncture. I am enclosing for your
                    information a copy of the memorandum. As I said above, it treats the general
                    aspects of the French situation and represents a symposium of the views of a
                    number of officials and political observers of different political
                        orientation.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d442-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>With all good wishes,</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d442-a1.xml" xpointer="d442-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d442-f1" n="1" xml:id="d442-f1-content">
                <p>The memorandum was prepared for use by Secretary Marshall as background for his
                    conversations at Paris en route to a meeting of the Council of Foreign Ministers
                    at Moscow. For the record of the Secretary’s conversation on March 6 with
                    Vincent Auriol, President of the French Republic, mostly with regard to the
                    forthcoming meeting at Moscow, see <ref target="frus1947v02#pg_190">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 190</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
